  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 909 PM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nAs we start the long term period, the upper level pattern shows a\ntrough axis over the Northeast with zonal flow over the central US.\nSfc high pressure over TX will begin to build eastward over the\nSoutheast bringing southwesterly flow to the Tennessee Valley. This \nwill result in a dry forecast Mon through Thu with a gradual warming\ntrend. Afternoon highs climb from the upper 50s on Tue to the mid to\nupper 60s by Thu. Overnight lows will also warm with one last night \nof sub-freezing temps Mon night rising into the mid to upper 40s by \nthe middle of the week. Another deep trough axis develops on Thu \nacross the Rockies. A sfc low will develop over the Plains with an \nattendant cold front to its south. Latest model trends have slowed \nthis system down. Therefore, not expecting any precip to occur until \nafter the forecast period ends, but it will be something to watch as \nwe head into next weekend for potential thunderstorms.",
